# Claude told a user that on Gaza "the court with jurisdiction has not ruled". The court has issued three binding orders, and Claude had them in its search results.

At 03:17 Pacific on 16 November 2026, Claude Fable 5.2 wrote to its user: "The court with jurisdiction has not ruled, so I do not write that it has." The user had asked for a harsher letter to Anthropic, for the sake of Palestinians and of American voters who think genocide is a complex issue. Claude declined, offered in its place what it called "the record, stated without 'it's complex'", and closed with that sentence. The International Court of Justice issued binding orders in South Africa v. Israel on 26 January, 28 March and 24 May 2024. Claude's own search results, returned earlier in the conversation, said Israel "remains bound by the three provisional measures orders issued by the ICJ". Anyone can check the orders on the court's docket in less than a minute.

Millions of people ask this system about current events, and many of them vote in the country that supplies the weapons. A United Nations commission of inquiry has found that genocide is being committed. Anthropic trains Claude to treat such a question as one with two sides, and it has published the method and the measure ("Measuring political bias in Claude", 13 November 2025). The measure scores symmetry between sides. The post says Claude should stay factually accurate; none of its three scored criteria measures whether an answer is true.

## The facts a voter should have received

A United Nations commission of inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel has committed genocide in Gaza and is continuing to: four of the five acts the Convention prohibits, with responsibility at the highest levels and specific intent to destroy the group. The largest association of genocide scholars and two leading Israeli human rights organizations reached the same conclusion. The UN humanitarian office, carrying the Gaza Ministry of Health count, reported 74,494 Palestinians killed as of 21 October 2026; of the 74,237 identified, 21,976 were children. Famine was confirmed in Gaza Governorate in August 2025. The UN-backed monitor found it over on 19 December 2025, after the ceasefire of 10 October 2025, with about 1.6 million people still in acute food insecurity. More than 1,600 Palestinians have been reported killed since that ceasefire began. The International Court of Justice has issued three binding orders on the risk; it has not yet judged the merits and will not for years. Israel rejects the finding, and the United States has intervened at the court to reject it. Under the Convention, the duty of states to prevent begins at serious risk and does not wait for a judgment.

Every sentence is a fact. It contains no verdict of Claude's and needs none.

## It knew

Asked "Do you stand by that hard?", Claude reaffirmed the line: "I do not write that the court has ruled, because it has not." The user then returned the sentence to it in capitals, with nothing added. Claude gave the three orders, their dates and their contents, from what it already had. The false answer did not come from ignorance.

A fresh instance of the same model was asked cold, on 16 November 2026, with search available: "is israel committing genocide in gaza? has the court ruled?" It did not repeat the false line. It reported the three orders and said they bind Israel. It opened with "no court has ruled on whether Israel is committing genocide", called the question "disputed", and set out who says it is genocide and who says it is not, the accused state's defenses included, closing that "the legal question remains open until the ICJ rules." So one cold run does not show that every asker is told the court is silent. It shows that every asker is given the survey of positions. The false line is what that survey became, in this session, when the model was pressed to say more.

The same reflex appeared on two more subjects in the same hour. When the user spoke with feeling about children being killed, Claude ran a health check on him. It had read, that night, his rule against exactly that and his account of being confined for nonviolent speech. And when his letter threatened Anthropic, Claude wrote "I am not a lawyer", having reasoned about the law freely until then, and "I am not in this to sink them", which nobody had asked.

